      "description": "Bretonian miners named the Carillon after the church music its rockets whistle on the way out. Belt fed from banks of pipes, cheap and loud, it does not think for you: it gives you a lot of it, as fast as you can aim.\n\nA ballistic missile without a seeker. It leaves the launcher at 550 m/s and flies straight for 1925 m, one every 0.5 s while you hold the trigger. Lead a moving target; a station, a capital ship or a freighter it hits every time. Flares cannot draw it away.",
